# S5-06 physical stand reachability probe, 2026-11-15

Purpose: verify SSH reachability before sending `guest/linux/tests/` and
`tests/fixtures/guest/stage5/` to the authorized temporary directory on the
physical Linux stand.

Worktree: `codex`, source revision `994d522`.
Target temporary directory: `/tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06-994d522`.

Command:

```sh
ssh -o ConnectTimeout=6 -o BatchMode=yes senya@192.168.1.14 \
  'mkdir -p /tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06-994d522'
```

Result: exit 255, `ssh: connect to host 192.168.1.14 port 22: Operation timed out`.
The connection did not reach SSH authentication or execute the remote command.
No files were transferred and no S5-06 physical checks were run by this attempt.

Next step: retry the authorized transfer/preflight when the stand or network route
is reachable. This probe is not guest-run or scenario acceptance evidence.

## Authorized transfer retry

After the owner explicitly authorized transfer, a second bounded attempt streamed
only `guest/linux/tests/` and `tests/fixtures/guest/stage5/` to
`/tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06` on the same host:

```sh
tar -czf - guest/linux/tests tests/fixtures/guest/stage5 |
  ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=12 -o ConnectionAttempts=1 \
    senya@192.168.1.14 \
    'mkdir -p /tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06 && tar -xzf - -C /tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06 && find /tmp/open-desktop-stage5-s5-06 -type f | wc -l'
```

Result: exit 255, `ssh: connect to host 192.168.1.14 port 22: Operation timed
out`. The connection again did not reach authentication or remote execution; no
files were transferred and this attempt ran no physical checks.
